      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To guard against supply chain volatility and price fluctuations in your MSA, you should prioritize binding delivery and substitution clauses that allow you to terminate contracts service to specific regions like your Munich facility. Include robust price adjustment mechanisms tied to inflation or standardized market indices, ensuring caps exist so you remain insulated from extreme spikes. Additionally, demand guarantees or standby clauses might be necessary, as these are rarely standard and can transfer production requirements to the supplier without triggering penalties.\n\n**One crucial legal disclaimer:** I am an AI, not an attorney, so please have specific Munich-based counsel review this draft, as German contract law (BGB) imposes significant liability caps and statutory warranties that could override standard international boilerplate language.",
