      "content": "To address hidden supply chain sabotage, your MSA should include a detailed \"Supply Chain Intermediaries\" clause requiring you to audit third-party logistics providers and demanding they be held jointly liable for any actions by those parties. You should also mandate a quarterly \"Supply Chain Integrity Audit\" giving your team unannounced access to their downstream inventory and delivery logs in targeted regions like Munich to verify consistency. Finally, include specific \"Anti-Sabotage\" provisions that trigger immediate termination rights if the supplier unlawfully interferes with ordered shipments or fails to honor agreed-upon service levels without valid cause.\n\n**Important Note:** Drafting provisions that explicitly define and sanction \"underhanded tactics\" can complicate enforcement, so consult a lawyer to ensure these terms align with German federal law while protecting your operational continuity.",
